# Old URLs -> current pages. Netlify serves these as HTTP 301s.
#
# First match wins, top to bottom: keep specific rules above general ones.
# `/x/*` also covers deeper paths; `:splat` carries the rest of the path over.
# Fragments (#anchor) never reach the server: browsers carry them across the
# 301, and anchors that moved off a page go in that page's `movedAnchors`
# frontmatter instead. `pnpm check-links` validates every rule here.

